                <pb facs="1004" n="966" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v04/pg966"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>On January 15, 1952, representatives of the United States and Ecuador initiated
                    negotiations at Quito for a bilateral military assistance agreement. Documents
                    pertaining to the negotiations are in Department of State file 722.5 MSP for
                    1952. For text of the Agreement, signed at Quito, February 20, 1952, and entered
                    into force on the same date, see Department of State Treaties and Other
                    International Acts Series (TIAS) No. 2560, or <hi rendition="#italic">United
                        States Treaties and Other International Agreements</hi> (UST), volume 3
                    (part 3), page 4162.</p>
                <p>Concurrent with the negotiations for the military assistance agreement,
                    representatives of the United States and Ecuador conducted negotiations for a
                    related bilateral military plan. The “Plan of the Governments of Ecuador and the
                    United States of America for Their Common Defense,” signed at Quito, February
                    20, 1952, and effective the same date, was transmitted to the Department of
                    State under cover of despatch 666, from Quito, dated February 20, 1952, not
                    printed (722.5 MSP/–2052).</p>
            </div>
